<article class="env-lemma" id="05SH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05SH">Lemma <span data-tag="05SH">4.22.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let $M : \mathcal{I} \to \mathcal{C}$ be a diagram with filtered (resp. cofiltered) index category $\mathcal{I}$. Let $F : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$ be a functor. If $M$ is essentially constant as an ind-object (resp. pro-object), then so is $F \circ M : \mathcal{I} \to \mathcal{D}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $X$ is a value for $M$, then it follows immediately from the definition that $F(X)$ is a value for $F \circ M$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>